# The PublicCMS UEditor controller's remote-image capture fetches each URL
# the editor supplies, sniffs the response stream to derive a file
# extension, and persists the stream into the site's web files whenever the
# sniff yields any extension at all -- so every fetchable content type,
# HTML and internal service responses included, is stored and handed back
# to the editor as an uploaded image (server-side request forgery with
# content persistence, CWE-918/CWE-436; issue #51). The gate in
# `catchimage` (publiccms-parent/publiccms-core/src/main/java/com/
# publiccms/controller/admin/sys/UeditorAdminController.java) reads:
#
#     FileType fileType = FileTypeDetector.detectFileType(inputStream);
#     String suffix = fileType.getCommonExtension();
#     if (CommonUtils.notEmpty(suffix)) { ... copyInputStreamToFile ... }
#
# The sniffing pair is the metadata-extractor library's documented API:
# `FileTypeDetector.detectFileType(InputStream)` types the stream and
# `FileType.getCommonExtension()` names the common extension of what it
# found. Commit 0f4c4872 keeps the fetch and adds the family restriction
# the feature implies -- `null != fileType.getMimeType() &&
# fileType.getMimeType().startsWith("image/")` joins the gate, and an empty
# result list now reports failure instead of success -- so a non-image
# response is still fetched but no longer persisted or announced.
#
# ## Measured at the current tip
#
# Three `--cache off` runs per revision over each full checkout (timeout
# 180, --max-ram 6GB): the controller carries one VYQL-INJ-001 row at
# :157-:164 and two VYQL-INJ-009 rows at both revisions, identical across
# the fix, plus one `core.ResourceRelease` flag on the try-with-resources
# close at :208 -- nothing on the fetch, the sniff or the persist in either
# the findings report or the `-flags only` view. The source half of the
# request-forgery chain is labelled (`request.getParameterValues` ->
# code.HttpInput at :210), but no Apache HttpClient call is bound: `HttpGet`
# construction and `HttpClient.execute` match none of the Java
# `code.UrlFetch` bindings (`openStream`, `openConnection`, `getForObject`,
# `getForEntity`), and `CmsFileUtils.copyInputStreamToFile` is bound as no
# sink. A fetch-side binding cannot discriminate this fix in principle --
# the fixed revision fetches the same unvalidated URLs and only the
# persistence is gated -- so the request-forgery detections that exist
# (VYQL-RF-001 taint, the fetch-guard review family) fire identically at
# both revisions even with the client bound.
#
# ## Why no binding ships
#
# The function context carries every call the gate uses, function-confined:
# throwaway probes over both revisions label `detectFileType`,
# `copyInputStreamToFile`, `HttpGet` and `getCommonExtension` at both, and
# `getMimeType` only at the fixed revision -- a clean discriminator, but it
# is the fixing commit's own API choice rather than the weakness. A probe
# binding `detectFileType` + `copyInputStreamToFile` under
# `not getMimeType/getContentType` on the three blocks below fires on the
# any-type gate, stays dark on the shipped fix, and fires on the third
# block: an extension allowlist restricting the persisted family to
# jpg/png/gif without ever reading the mime type, an equally-valid
# remediation the mime-read negation cannot see (an enum-membership gate
# `fileType == FileType.JPEG` produces no call token at all). The general
# condition -- the sniffed type is consulted but never restricted to the
# family the feature promises -- has no token-level expression that is not
# an enumeration of remediation spellings, and each spelling missed
# mislabels a correctly-fixed variant.
#
# The shape also holds no second instance to measure precision on: across
# 60,856 Java files in the local clone corpus, `detectFileType` occurs in
# exactly this target's two revisions, `guessContentTypeFromStream`,
# `getContentTypeFor` and `MimetypesFileTypeMap` in none, and
# `probeContentType` only inside the Tika library's own detector
# implementation -- a consumer nowhere. A concept minted for a population
# of one tree would be inert everywhere else, and no existing concept
# carries the semantics: `IncompleteFileExtensionValidation` is the other
# axis of the same trust decision (admission on the sniffed extension while
# the client-declared one goes unread, a documented pair on the
# uploaded-file classes), `UnsanitizedSvgUpload` is domain-locked to SVG
# sanitisers, and the request-forgery guard family is fetch-side.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, all three tests
# rejected. Tests 1 and 2 pin the revision pair; test 3 pins the bar any
# future detection must clear: when fetched-content family-restriction
# vocabulary lands, test 1 flips to expect while tests 2 and 3 stay reject
# -- a detection keyed on the mime read alone fails test 3, which is why
# none ships today.

test "rank1614: fetched content saves with any detected type"
  lang java
  file publiccms-parent/publiccms-core/src/main/java/com/publiccms/controller/admin/sys/UeditorAdminController.java
  reject VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  package com.publiccms.controller.admin.sys;

  import java.io.BufferedInputStream;
  import java.util.ArrayList;
  import java.util.List;
  import java.util.Map;

  import com.drew.imaging.FileType;
  import com.drew.imaging.FileTypeDetector;

  public class UeditorAdminController {

      public Map<String, Object> catchimage(HttpServletRequest request) throws Exception {
          try (CloseableHttpClient httpclient = HttpClients.custom()
                  .setDefaultRequestConfig(CommonConstants.defaultRequestConfig).build();) {
              String[] files = request.getParameterValues(FIELD_NAME + "[]");
              if (CommonUtils.notEmpty(files)) {
                  List<Map<String, Object>> list = new ArrayList<>();
                  for (String image : files) {
                      HttpGet httpget = new HttpGet(image);
                      CloseableHttpResponse response = httpclient.execute(httpget);
                      HttpEntity entity = response.getEntity();
                      if (null != entity) {
                          BufferedInputStream inputStream = new BufferedInputStream(entity.getContent());
                          FileType fileType = FileTypeDetector.detectFileType(inputStream);
                          String suffix = fileType.getCommonExtension();
                          if (CommonUtils.notEmpty(suffix)) {
                              String fileName = CmsFileUtils.getUploadFileName(suffix);
                              String filePath = siteComponent.getWebFilePath(site, fileName);
                              CmsFileUtils.copyInputStreamToFile(inputStream, filePath);
                              list.add(getResultMap(true));
                          }
                      }
                      EntityUtils.consume(entity);
                  }
                  Map<String, Object> map = getResultMap(true);
                  map.put("list", list);
                  return map;
              }
          } catch (Exception e) {
              log.error(e.getMessage(), e);
              return getResultMap(false);
          }
          return getResultMap(false);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1614: the fixed revision saves images only"
